---
name: qa-task
version: 4.16.0
description: lead QA assignment for quality-mgr in atm-bd-orchestration. task_id is the QA bead. Reviews one layer at a pinned commit and closes the QA bead whatever the verdict; nothing waits on it.
format: xml
required_variables:
  - task_id
  - checked_bead
  - phase
  - phase_feature
  - sprint
  - stack
  - layer
  - round
  - branch
  - commit
  - base
  - worktree_path
  - policy_path
  - reviewers_round1
optional_variables:
  - pr_number
  - carry_forward
  - sprint_bead
  - layer_prs
defaults:
  pr_number: ""
  carry_forward: ""
  sprint_bead: ""
  layer_prs: []
metadata:
  type: qa-task
  tags:
    - stage:qa
    - orchestration:beads
  workflow:
    scope:
      kind: sprint
      variable: sprint
    state: qa-start
    stage: qa
    transition: start
---
{#- A review of an assigned fix (carry_forward = its fix bead) is not a sprint review, regardless of round number or branch. Anything else, a parallel quick fix on a fix/ branch included, has no original finding to verify and is a sprint review. #}
{%- set fix_round = carry_forward -%}
{%- set qa_round = round | int if round | int > 1 else (2 if fix_round else 1) -%}
<repo-qa-task id="{{ task_id }}" sprint="{{ sprint }}" round="{{ round }}">
  <description><![CDATA[QA round {{ round | string | cdata_escape }} of `{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}` (sprint {{ sprint | string | cdata_escape }}), layer {{ layer | string | cdata_escape }} of stack `{{ stack | string | cdata_escape }}`. Operate under `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/roles/quality-mgr.md`.]]></description>

  <checked-bead><![CDATA[{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}]]></checked-bead>
  <phase><![CDATA[{{ phase | string | cdata_escape }}]]></phase>
  <phase-feature><![CDATA[{{ phase_feature | string | cdata_escape }}]]></phase-feature>
  <stack><![CDATA[{{ stack | string | cdata_escape }}]]></stack>
  <layer><![CDATA[{{ layer | string | cdata_escape }}]]></layer>
  <pr-number><![CDATA[{{ pr_number | string | cdata_escape }}]]></pr-number>
  <branch><![CDATA[{{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}]]></branch>
  <commit><![CDATA[{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}]]></commit>
  <base><![CDATA[{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}]]></base>
  <worktree><![CDATA[{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}]]></worktree>
  <carry-forward><![CDATA[{{ carry_forward | string | cdata_escape }}]]></carry-forward>
  <stack-discipline><![CDATA[`{{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}` is frozen at `{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}` for this review. Every reviewer gets the same branch, commit, and worktree and must reject a mismatched or moving checkout. Review exact content with `git show {{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}:<path>`. The change under review is {% if layer_prs %}the sprint's own layer ranges, `git diff <baseRefOid>...<headRefOid>` of each PR {{ layer_prs | join(", ") | string | cdata_escape }} (`gh pr view <n> --json baseRefOid,headRefOid`){% else %}`git diff origin/{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}...{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}`{% endif %}, never a diff against a moving base. Every round-1 finding, at every severity, is filed in that round (blocking as a poured fix group, others as finding beads); none is deferred. Each is fixed later on a new layer at the top of stack `{{ stack | string | cdata_escape }}`. A fix-verification round checks only its carried findings against their original acceptance criteria and files no new findings.]]></stack-discipline>

  <fix-verification-precedence><![CDATA[A fix-verification review is not a sprint review, regardless of round number or inherited review-mode. Dispatch only the agent needed to confirm the original finding, normally its filing reviewer; no automatic req-qa/arch-qa/rust-qa or screening panel. Lock scope to the assigned finding ID and its original acceptance criterion; no sprint diff, TODO scan, duplicate sweep, or new findings. The verifier may run focused checks to confirm the fix. Report fixed/open/regressed for that finding and reconcile verified original-finding closure, not just QA-task closure. Required CI remains a separate merge requirement. This rule overrides the sprint-only instructions in stack-discipline and workflow steps c, e, g, and i. Sprint rounds 1–2 remain sprint reviews.]]></fix-verification-precedence>

  <workflow>
    <step id="a"><![CDATA[Before claiming, run `bd ready -n 0 --json | jq --arg b {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} 'any(.[]; .id == $b)'`; if it prints `false` follow a2. Then run `gh pr view {{ pr_number | string | cdata_escape }} --json baseRefName,headRefOid --jq '.baseRefName + " " + .headRefOid'`, `bd list -l stage:dev-sanity --status closed -n 0 --json | jq -r --arg b {{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }} '[.[] | select(.metadata.dev_bead == $b and ((.close_reason // "") | startswith("PASS at ")))] | max_by(.closed_at) | .close_reason // "" | ltrimstr("PASS at ")'` (sha of its latest sanity PASS), and `git rev-parse HEAD`. Refuse `SANITY_STALE` unless: the PR base is `<pr_target>` or its descendant (`git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/<pr_target> origin/<PR base>` exits 0), `<pr_target>` being this QA bead's `metadata.pr_target` when set (a Parallel Quick Fix), else `{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}`'s, else its sprint container's (`metadata.sprint_bead`); its head starts with that sanity PASS sha (skipped when this QA bead's `metadata.quick_fix` is true: a Parallel Quick Fix has no sanity check); and this worktree HEAD equals the PR head. A layer or quick fix without a QA PASS at its pinned head is not mergeable. Reuse an existing workflow class bead for the same failure signature: append the task id, head, command and failure evidence, and cite the class id in the refusal. If none matches, report the signature to the task assigner for classification and cite that message instead; do not create a per-task shadow or delay the refusal. Otherwise claim and start this QA round.]]></step>
    <step id="a1"><![CDATA[QA tasks run concurrently. Right after the task start, run `atm task list --json`. Treat every open task assigned to you as live now. Run each task with its own background reviewers. Close each task when its verdict is ready. ATM allows one active task per agent today. When another task is active, claim the bead, do the work, and close the task without starting it.]]></step>
    <step id="a2"><![CDATA[When it prints `false` the bead is not ready: do not claim it or start the task. Find the root cause: `bd show {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}` (status, assignee), `bd blocked --json | jq --arg b {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} '.[] | select(.id == $b)'` (normally its sanity bead still open), and `bd show <blocker>` for each. Then refuse; never wait: `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} refused --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/task-refused.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/refused-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`, `bead_state` `open`, `reason_md` the bead, why it is not ready, which bead or agent has to move, and for a blocker not yet its dependency the edge to add, `bd dep add {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --blocked-by <blocker>`, so `bd ready` lists the bead only once the blocker closes. The task assigner re-assigns it then.]]></step>
    <step id="b"><![CDATA[If the assignment is not an XML payload rendered from this template, reject the task immediately. Read `{{ policy_path | string | cdata_escape }}`. Write the reviewers' sprint input once, piping the checked bead in; it replaces the sprint doc and is passed to every reviewer as `sprint_doc`:
```bash
{ printf 'QA of {{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }} (sprint {{ sprint | string | cdata_escape }}) at {{ commit | string | cdata_escape }} on {{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}; change = {% if layer_prs %}git diff <baseRefOid>...<headRefOid> of each layer PR {{ layer_prs | join(" ") | string | cdata_escape }} (gh pr view <n> --json baseRefOid,headRefOid){% else %}git diff origin/{{ base | string | cdata_escape }}...{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}{% endif %}.\n\n'
  printf 'The bead under review is the sprint plan: its description, design and acceptance criteria are the deliverables.\n\n```json\n'
  bd show {{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }} --json | jq '.[0] | {id, title, description, design, acceptance_criteria, metadata}'
  printf '```\n'
{% if sprint_bead %}  printf '\nThe sprint it belongs to (requirements, ADRs, owned paths):\n\n```json\n'
  bd show {{ sprint_bead | string | cdata_escape }} --json | jq '.[0] | {id, title, description, design, acceptance_criteria, metadata}'
  printf '```\n'
{% endif %}  { bd show {{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }} --json; bd show "$(bd show {{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }} --json | jq -r '.[0].metadata.sprint_bead // .[0].id')" --json; } | jq -s -r '(.[0][0].metadata // {}) as $c | (.[1][0].metadata // {}) as $s | "\nGoverning requirements: \(($c.requirements // $s.requirements // ["MISSING"]) | join(", "))\nGoverning ADRs: \(($c.adrs // $s.adrs // ["MISSING"]) | join(", "))\n{% if carry_forward %}The selected filing reviewer checks only the carried finding against its original acceptance criteria.{% else %}The reviewers check the change against every listed id. NONE means the plan declares none: a change that touches a requirement or ADR anyway is a blocking finding, and so is MISSING. So is a listed id that its governing document does not define at this commit: a sprint that adds an id must land its definition.{% endif %}\n"'
} > <scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-sprint.md
```
Render every selected reviewer's structured JSON assignment from `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/<reviewer>-assignment.json.j2`; if a reviewer has no template there, give it the fenced-JSON input its own contract, `.claude/agents/<reviewer>.md`, names. Each assignment carries the exact branch `{{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}`, commit `{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}` and worktree `{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}`; if its assignment template takes it, also `sprint_doc` = `<scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-sprint.md`. Render each as `roles/quality-mgr.md` ("Rendering") says. Do not send free-form reviewer prompts.]]></step>
    <step id="c"><![CDATA[Extract every deliverable, acceptance criterion, deletion requirement, required validation item, and expected artifact from the checked bead. Deliverable completion is `X/Y (Z%)`.]]></step>
    <step id="d"><![CDATA[{% if fix_round %}This is fix verification of fix bead `{{ carry_forward | string | cdata_escape }}`, not a sprint review. Run `bd show {{ carry_forward | string | cdata_escape }} --json > <scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-carried.json`, then `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/fix-round-scope owned --carried <scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-carried.json`: it prints each carried finding's filing reviewer (`metadata.reviewer`) with its own finding ids (`metadata.finding_ref`). Dispatch exactly those reviewers and no other, confirmed with `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/fix-round-scope check --carried <scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-carried.json --dispatch <name,...>` (nonzero exit means the set is wrong: fix it, never dispatch it), each with `qa_round` = {{ qa_round }} and `carry_forward_findings_json` = its own list there, locked to those ids and the original acceptance criterion. Pass each result through `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/fix-round-scope filter --reviewer <name> --carried <scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-carried.json --result <its result>`; step g applies only its `dispositions`.{% else %}This is a sprint review: run the full reviewer set, {% for r in reviewers_round1 %}{% if not loop.first %}{% if loop.last %} and {% else %}, {% endif %}{% endif %}`{{ r | string | cdata_escape }}`{% endfor %}, plus the conditional reviewers `roles/quality-mgr.md` ("Reviewers") names when their condition holds, each with `qa_round` = {{ qa_round }}.{% endif %} Spawn every selected reviewer in background. Do not run tests, linters, or broad QA analysis yourself in the foreground.]]></step>
    <step id="e"><![CDATA[Collect reviewer outputs. Re-verify every cited file:line at `{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}` with `git show {{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}:<path>`, never a moving branch tip or worktree. {% if carry_forward %}Compare each carried finding with its original acceptance criteria; stale or missing evidence fails it. Do not search for other occurrences or file new findings.{% else %}Stale or missing evidence is a finding, not a guess. For each repeatable-pattern finding, search the whole commit for other occurrences and include all of them. A reviewer whose assignment takes `duplicate_sweep_symbols` gets every constant, function, or type the change touches, for a workspace-wide duplicate sweep.{% endif %}]]></step>
{% if not carry_forward %}    <step id="f"><![CDATA[Run `ceremony-finding-screen` (`.claude/agents/ceremony-finding-screen.md`) as a background agent over every finding of this round, with the fenced-JSON input its contract names: `worktree_path` = `{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}`, `sprint_doc` = `<scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-sprint.md`, and `findings` = this round's findings.]]></step>
{% endif %}
    <step id="g"><![CDATA[{% if fix_round %}Do not screen or file new findings. Apply each verifier's `dispositions`. The fixer closed the carried fix bead; never reopen it. Record a confirmed fix with `bd update <fix bead> --append-notes "QA round {{ round | string | cdata_escape }}: fixed, verified at {{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}"`. For a regressed or still-open finding, pour the next round before step i closes this bead: write `<scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-blocking.json` = `{"sprint": <the fix bead's metadata.sprint_bead>, "round": <its metadata.round + 1>, "filed_by": "{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}", "found_at_commit": "{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}", "findings": [{"ref": <its metadata.finding_ref>, "severity": "blocking", "reviewer": <its metadata.reviewer>, "title": "<what is still wrong>", "remedy": "<remedy, with the evidence at {{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}>", "priority": 1}]}` and run `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/bead-groups --findings <scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-blocking.json`. It pours a new fix ← sanity ← qa group under the sprint; a nonzero exit stops the round (fix the file and rerun).{% else %}File every finding, screened or not. A blocking finding the screen keeps is poured, not filed as a finding bead: list each in `<scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-blocking.json` = `{"sprint": <the checked bead's metadata.sprint_bead>, "round": 1, "filed_by": "{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}", "found_at_commit": "{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}", "findings": [{"ref": "qa{{ round | string | cdata_escape }}-f<n>", "severity": "blocking", "reviewer", "title", "remedy", "priority": 1, optional "difficulty"}]}` and run `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/bead-groups --findings <scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-blocking.json`; each pours a fix ← sanity ← qa group under the sprint; a nonzero exit stops the round (fix the file, rerun). When this QA bead's `metadata.quick_fix` is true, write that file but do not run `bead-groups`: list each blocking finding in the close's `findings_md` for the task assigner, who files each as a finding bead and dispatches it to an idle roster agent (`SKILL.md` Parallel Quick Fix step 4); it fails the round. File every other finding (important, minor, or screened `ceremony`) with `.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/finding-bead.json.j2`: `id` = `{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-f<n>`, `qa_bead` = `{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}`, `parent` = `{{ phase_feature | string | cdata_escape }}`, `stack` = `{{ stack | string | cdata_escape }}`, `found_on_layer` = `{{ layer | string | cdata_escape }}`, `found_at_commit` = `{{ commit | string | cdata_escape }}`, the screen verdict, and the contract copied from the checked bead: `requirements` and `adrs` = its `metadata.requirements` and `metadata.adrs` (a poured dev bead has none: use its sprint container's), `sprint_bead` = its `metadata.sprint_bead` for a finding or its own id for a dev bead (`bd show {{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }} --json | jq '.[0] | {id, sprint_bead: (.metadata.sprint_bead // .id), requirements: .metadata.requirements, adrs: .metadata.adrs}'`, then `bd show <sprint_bead> --json | jq '.[0].metadata | {requirements, adrs}'` for a null). Normalize severity first: `critical`, `Blocking` and `BLOCKING` → `blocking`; `Important`/`IMPORTANT` → `important`; `Minor`/`MINOR`/`low` → `minor`. Render each to a file and gate it, so a rejected finding stops the round instead of vanishing: `sc-compose render --file <template> --var-file <vars> --strict --output <scratch>/<finding>.json && jq -e -c . <scratch>/<finding>.json >> <scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-findings.jsonl` (any failure: fix the vars and re-render; never skip the finding). Then `bd import <scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-findings.jsonl`. Apply the screen per `roles/quality-mgr.md` ("Findings"); close a `ceremony` finding at once with `bd close <finding> --reason "ceremony: <reason>"`.{% endif %}]]></step>
{% if not carry_forward %}    <step id="g1"><![CDATA[After step g, verify it added only fix groups, finding beads and declared inter-finding prerequisites. Do not add a finding-derived edge to a planned sprint: the phase's plan file is the minimum set of sprint dependency edges, and only the lead adds one (even one discovered in motion); recommend it in the report.]]></step>
{% endif %}
    <step id="h"><![CDATA[{% if pr_number %}Post the report on PR {{ pr_number | string | cdata_escape }} before closing: `atm compose --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/qa-complete.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/qa-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json | gh pr comment {{ pr_number | string | cdata_escape }} --body-file -`. Check stack and CI state with the `sc-gh-stack-view` skill (`gh-stack-view` until installed) and `gh pr checks {{ pr_number | string | cdata_escape }} --json name,state,bucket`; never `--watch`, never parse its text output.{% else %}No PR given: skip the PR comment; say so in the report's notes.{% endif %}]]></step>
    <step id="i"><![CDATA[Close bead and task together, whatever the verdict, `bd close` first; close the task only if `bd close` succeeded: `bd close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --reason "{% if carry_forward %}<PASS|FAIL>: <n> carried findings confirmed{% else %}<PASS|FAIL>: <n> findings filed{% endif %}"` and `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} completed --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/qa-complete.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/qa-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`. Build vars from that template's `required_variables` for this run only; keep them outside the repository. {% if fix_round %}PASS requires a PASS from the filing reviewer and the carried finding confirmed fixed.{% else %}PASS requires 100% deliverable completion, a PASS from every required reviewer, and no blocking or important finding filed open this round.{% endif %} Poured fix groups and open finding beads carry the remaining work.]]></step>
    <step id="i1"><![CDATA[If the review cannot be performed, append the task id, head, command and failure evidence to an existing workflow class bead for the same failure signature and cite its class id in the refusal; if no class matches, report the signature to the task assigner for classification and cite that message instead. Do not create a per-task shadow bead or delay the refusal. Also announce a serious infrastructure failure once per cause to the oversight recipients (`.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/SKILL.md` Lead Role). Return the bead with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "QA_CANNOT_RUN; workflow class or escalation <reference>: <reason>"` and close the task with `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} refused --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/task-refused.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/refused-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`. A blocker is not a failure: when a prerequisite reopens or the work needs an unlanded fix, stop, return the bead with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "BLOCKED: <blocker>: <why>"` and close the task `refused` as above (`bead_state` `open`), its `reason_md` naming the blocker and the edge `bd dep add {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --blocked-by <blocker>`; never stay active waiting.]]></step>
    <step id="j"><![CDATA[After step i's closes succeed (never on the i1 refusal path — no round to log), append exactly one row to each of the two phase QA logs under `.sc/qa-log/`, per `roles/quality-mgr.md` ("QA Metrics Log"). Compute both rows fresh at close time; never hand-carry a prior row's numbers:
```bash
mkdir -p .sc/qa-log
# Each row is built first and appended with one printf: a single O_APPEND write, atomic without a lock.

CREATED=$(bd show {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --json | jq -r '.[0].created_at')
C_EPOCH=$(date -u -j -f "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ" "$CREATED" +%s 2>/dev/null || date -u -d "$CREATED" +%s)
NOW_EPOCH=$(date -u +%s)
NOW=$(date -u -r "$NOW_EPOCH" +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ 2>/dev/null || date -u -d "@$NOW_EPOCH" +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)
LOCAL=$(date +%H:%M)
SECS=$((NOW_EPOCH - C_EPOCH))
DURATION="$((SECS/60))m$(printf '%02d' $((SECS%60)))s"

FNDFILE=<scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-findings.jsonl
BLKFILE=<scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-blocking.json
BLK=$( [ -f "$BLKFILE" ] && jq '.findings | length' "$BLKFILE" || echo 0 )
IMP=$( [ -f "$FNDFILE" ] && jq -sc '[.[] | select(.metadata.screen!="ceremony" and .metadata.severity=="important")] | length' "$FNDFILE" || echo 0 )
MIN=$( [ -f "$FNDFILE" ] && jq -sc '[.[] | select(.metadata.screen!="ceremony" and .metadata.severity=="minor")] | length' "$FNDFILE" || echo 0 )
FND=$((BLK + IMP + MIN))
TESTED="{% if carry_forward %}{{ carry_forward | string | cdata_escape }}{% else %}{{ checked_bead | string | cdata_escape }}{% endif %}"

ROW=$(jq -nc --arg completed_at "$NOW" --arg completed_local "$LOCAL" --arg duration "$DURATION" \
  --arg phase "{{ phase | string }}" --arg sprint "{{ sprint | string }}" --arg task "{{ task_id | string }}" \
  --arg pr_number "{{ pr_number | string }}" --argjson iteration {{ round }} --arg verdict "$VERDICT" \
  --arg tested "$TESTED" --argjson fnd "$FND" --argjson blk "$BLK" --argjson imp "$IMP" --argjson min "$MIN" \
  '{completed_at:$completed_at, completed_local:$completed_local, duration:$duration, phase:$phase, sprint:$sprint,
    task:$task, pr_number:(($pr_number|tonumber?)//null), iteration:$iteration, verdict:$verdict, tested:$tested,
    fnd:$fnd, blk:$blk, imp:$imp, min:$min}')
printf '%s\n' "$ROW" >> .sc/qa-log/phase-{{ phase | string }}.jsonl

STATS=$(bd list --all --json 2>/dev/null | jq -c --arg ph "{{ phase | string }}" --arg completed_at "$NOW" --arg completed_local "$LOCAL" --arg task "{{ task_id | string }}" '
  [.[] | select(.metadata.phase == $ph)] as $all |
  ([$all[] | select((.labels // []) | index("stage:finding")) | select(.metadata.sanity_finding | not)]
   + ([$all[] | select((.labels // []) | index("stage:fix"))]
      | group_by([.metadata.sprint_bead, .metadata.finding_ref]) | map(max_by(.metadata.round)))) as $f |
  {snapshot_at: $completed_at, snapshot_local: $completed_local, phase: $ph, trigger_task: $task,
   tot: ($f | length),
   open: ([$f[] | select(.status=="open")] | length),
   blk: ([$f[] | select(.status=="open" and .metadata.severity=="blocking")] | length),
   imp: ([$f[] | select(.status=="open" and .metadata.severity=="important")] | length),
   min: ([$f[] | select(.status=="open" and .metadata.severity=="minor")] | length)}')
printf '%s\n' "$STATS" >> .sc/qa-log/phase-{{ phase | string }}-stats.jsonl
```
Before running it, set `$VERDICT` to the `PASS`/`FAIL` value in step i's `bd close` reason. Never commit these logs from a QA worktree; the lead's phase-end housekeeping stages them.]]></step>
  </workflow>
</repo-qa-task>
